6-51bc-b2f0-92e3d909f299" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054936 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186055548 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054936 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186055549 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054936 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186055550 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054936 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054936 #edb/ref 1045 "Absolute Value Expressions" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054936 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186055548 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054936 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186049844 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054936 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "0b4acd9e-f257-5db1-a9ff-f4bc70fb528a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055103 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186052049 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055103 #edb/ref 1069 "q-212318" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055103 #edb/ref 1071 "If $t = 0$, then $\\begin{vmatrix}t - 2 & -\\end{vmatrix}t + 3|=$ {{field-1}}." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055103 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "77b7fa26-d28f-58ff-acd8-77ebdc7f46c6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055548 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186055549 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055548 #edb/ref 1061 147765 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055548 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "2ecbe2d3-3bf6-5c94-9e47-13b35a557d38" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055548 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186056066 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055549 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186055550 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055549 #edb/ref 1061 147766 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055549 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "4957b9ec-7c2c-553a-b341-f367fd1d5e59" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055549 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186054626 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055550 #edb/ref 1061 147770 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055550 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "ea43903e-13f4-5326-a1ae-670194c48ad9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055550 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186054627 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186056066 #edb/ref 1064 "Let's take a number, say, $-3$. We can depict it on a number line as follows:\n\n![](images/de/ded8743284f207bff35eba24617fd4245a69d439ed151d09eed564813f9d72fb.png)\n\nThe *distance* between the number $-3$ and $0$ is known as the **absolute value** of $-3$. We write it as\n\n$$\n\\mid -3 \\mid = {\\color{red}3}\n$$\n\nSimilarly, $\\mid \\,2\\, \\mid$, the absolute value of the number $2$, is the distance between $2$ and $0$:\n\n![](images/f4/f44fcd05fb0932083d48c8b11892247d8de8fbc46ccf7186fb12843702181aea.png)\n\nWe write\n\n$$\n\\mid \\,2\\, \\mid = {\\color{red}2}\n$$\n\nSo, the absolute value simply\n\n- *removes the minus sign*, if the number is negative, or\n- does nothing, if the number is non-negative.\n\nSometimes, we can be asked to evaluate an expression involving the absolute value function, like $\\mid x +1 \\mid + 5$ when $x=-3$. In this case, we evaluate the expression inside the absolute value before simplifying the rest of the expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mid x + 1 \\mid + 5 &=  \\\\\n\\mid (-3) + 1 \\mid + 5 &=  \\\\\n\\mid - 2 \\mid + 5 &=  \\\\\n2 + 5 &=  \\\\\n&= 7\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186056066 #edb/ref 1065 8817 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186056066 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "3325f9a7-d389-562e-ac1b-4eb26671f84b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186056066 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
